Test Case: other_allow_extension_operations_disabled_without_vm_agent
================================================================================

Initial Error:
Error: Attempt to get attribute from null value

  on azapi.tf line 53, in resource "azapi_resource" "this":
  53:       type         = identity.value.type
     ├────────────────
     │ identity.value is null

This value is null, so it does not have any attributes.

Fix Process:

Attempt 1:
- Problem Analysis: The azurerm.tf.bak has no identity block, so module.replicator.azapi_header.identity is null. The can() function returns true for null values, causing the for_each to iterate with a null value.
- Fix Method: Change the condition to check if identity is not null using try() with a default of null, then check if result is not null
- Changes Made: Update dynamic identity block condition from `can(module.replicator.azapi_header.identity)` to `module.replicator.azapi_header.identity != null`
- Result: Success - terraform plan now works and shows acceptable drifts only (ignore_null_property, locks, output, replace_triggers_external_values, sensitive_body_version, type, timeouts, and body properties that are Optional+Computed fields)

